{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c7d2f3a6a14efd61","name":"Toscan 8-Q Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-c7d2f3a6a14efd61","title":"Toscan 8-Q Starfighter","revision":19594,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:15:05Z","sha256":"376aaaa4f242ad0a7ac95a10b338df16f6eb64bbb855323b9e3123b345cb09da","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19594","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Toscan%208-Q%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c7d2f3a6a14efd61","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Built by Shobquix Yards (using a cockpit designed by Koensayr and later appearing on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Y-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Y-Wing"},"), the Toscan 8-Q Starfighter was designed well before ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," as an open-frame ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," for other shipyards. The base model, the Toscan 8-Q, has a Class 2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},", weak shields, basic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"},", and life support for a pilot installed, but carries only a basic weapon package of two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Extensive room is left for heavier weapons, more crew space, additional maneuvering thrusters, greater cargo capacity, or whatever other improvements are desired. The idea was that other shipyards would buy the Toscan and make whatever modifications were required to fill various ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," roles. Expecting huge sales numbers, Shobquix produced the Toscan frame in enormous numbers. Overall, the program was a horrible failure.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The problems with the idea were twofold. First, most shipyards prefer to custom-design their own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," frames from the ground up. Second, the cost of a modified Toscan (with both Shobquix and whoever \"finished\" the Starfighter taking a profit) was too high compared to its final capabilities. A few hundred were bought by various shipyards as testing craft (Sienar in particular built several Gunship Toscans, with Quad ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," and Dual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannons"}," as test beds for systems later added to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["GAT-12 Skipray Blastboat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/GAT-12_Skipray_Blastboat"},"), but most were sold at discount to private buyers. Such Toscans rarely live up to their potential (since private buyers lack the resources of a full shipyard), but most could at least add some cargo and passenger capacity. The statistics here represent a \"typical\" Toscan, though many can be found with both heavier and lighter weapon loads.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Toscan 8-Q Starfighter Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +3; ",{"